From 45309ded4f69cdb5458b6b54de65f2db5e23e6d9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 23:39:51 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Add Esc-B early stopping on top of the Wii oracle

Esc (Wang et al., PVLDB 2025), variant without index interaction:
checked at the start of every Phase-2 greedy step of two-phase greedy,
stops when eta_U(final best) - eta_L(best so far) <= epsilon.
- selection/esc.py: EarlyStoppingChecker (simulated greedy on derived costs
  for eta_L; Eq. 10 top-K sum of workload-level MCI bounds for eta_U)
- two-phase greedy: parameters esc ("none"/"esc_b"), esc_epsilon, esc_clamp
- budget_aware.py: need_omega so Omega costs exist also without Wii; hook
  in the greedy loop
- scripts/wii_experiments.py: "esc" experiment; scripts/esc_summary.py
- tests/test_esc.py: synthetic-cost tests (loss <= epsilon, bound validity)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CjHr7mFBfqBd1hBxcjucKr
